CHAPTER V
OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 30
protection of women victims of violence, the Regional Government is obligated to:
a. guarantee the implementation of the fulfillment of women's rights and the provision of assurance of safety from acts of violence, and efforts to prevent exploitation of women in the region;
b. establish policies, programs, activities for the protection of women and guarantees for victim handling to eliminate all forms of discrimination and acts of violence against women in the region;
c. provide guidance and supervision in efforts to protect women carried out by Regional Apparatus handling the Protection and Empowerment of Women;
d. endeavor to establish women's protection institutions;
e. establish policies, programs and activities for the protection of women that have been determined; and
f. conduct socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of women victims of violence and discrimination;

Article 4
Every Female victim of violence has the right to:
a. obtain protection;
b. obtain determine her own decisions;
c. obtain information;
d. obtain complaint handling;
e. obtain assistance;
f. obtain continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage; and
g. obtain confidential handling both from individuals, groups or institutions both government and non-government.

